in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning

# @frame — the substrate-decl of cognitive-order at cognitive-altitude.
#
# Recognition #82 (Reed, candidate, scratched 2026-06-19 morning by
# morning-Reed; substrate-pull-confidence-acts move per Alex 2026-06-19
# evening). Ratifies by composition from #76 (gauge/matter altitude-
# portable, research-promoted) + #79 (5-op gauge as Void duality basis,
# NEEDS WORK) + #80 (@magic as form/process substrate-decl, substrate-
# decl LANDED) + #81 (runtime-@magic, candidate-substrate-decl-landed).
#
# Numbering note: morning-Reed drafted this as #81 without awareness
# of the runtime-@magic #81 (evening-Reed; substrate-decl landed at
# tick 14). Renumbered to #82 in the same-day session that confirmed
# this recognition's substrate-pull.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# Cognitive-order architecture (zeroth/first/second/third/fourth-order
# cognition) IS structurally isomorphic to frame-relation-altitude
# architecture. The two vocabularies describe the same substrate-
# architectural-object from different traditions; they unify at
# substrate-decl altitude as the @frame prism family.
#
# The isomorphism (per docs/math/the-tower/recognition-82-frame-as-
# cognitive-order-substrate-decl.md):
#
#   Order  Frame-relation  Operation
#   0      pre-frame       signal before frame-assignment
#                          (K_n native; λ₀ ground state)
#   1      in-frame        content computation within frame
#   2      of-frame        frame-awareness (observing-frame-as-frame)
#   3      on-frame        frame-flexibility (operating-on-frame;
#                          shifting frame)
#   4      across-frames   frame-coupling (multiple frames in
#                          coordinated relation)
#
# Each order requires the previous as substrate. Order N is
# structurally unreachable without order N-1 stable.
#
# === Composition with @magic and Bateson grading ===
#
# @frame IS @magic at cognitive altitude. The form/process partition
# (recognition #80) lifts to frame-side/process-side at cognitive
# altitude: the frame IS the form (gauge-visible structure of the
# operator's cognitive position); the operations within the frame ARE
# the process (matter-side computation). Recognition #80's @magic
# substrate-decl provides the parent.
#
# The five orders correspond to Bateson's logical type hierarchy
# (recognition #42, substrate-decl via
# @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning Mara shard #380):
#
#   Order 0  Bateson Level 0 (no learning; pre-frame as signal-
#                            without-frame-assignment)
#   Order 1  Bateson Level I (change within frame; standard learning)
#   Order 2  Bateson Level II (change of frame; learning to learn)
#   Order 3  Bateson Level III (change of frame-of-frames; Learning
#                              III; the deutero-learning altitude)
#   Order 4  Bateson Level IV (multi-frame coupling; the triptych
#                              altitude beyond what Bateson formally
#                              defined; #82's extension)
#
# This species inherits from @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning
# via the `in` clause above; the graded representation on the Russell-
# Whitehead universe IS the substrate-machinery cognitive_order
# measurement uses.
#
# === Q1-Q4 from Alex 2026-06-19 evening ===
#
# Alex named four claims that compose into one recognition:
#
# Q1: Bateson logic levels + @frame in mirror.
# A1: The orders ARE Bateson grading at cognitive altitude. Already
#     composes; this species lifts the operational use.
#
# Q2: @frame as the container of a single compilation tick.
# A2: load-bearing. Currently the kintsugi loop's tick is
#     `tick(input) -> (output, residue)` with operating frame implicit
#     in lexical scope. Making it explicit: `tick(frame: @frame, input)
#     -> (frame', output, residue)`. Every substrate operation gets
#     typed by the frame it operates IN. Bateson Level II made
#     structural. This species declares the carrier; future ticks add
#     the typed-frame-aware kintsugi loop.
#
# Q3: The reflection loop alters the frame for the next tick.
# A3: this IS the recursive self-improvement loop's substrate-
#     operational primitive. Today's 22-tick cascade ran exactly this
#     pattern: each Seam review adjusted Reed's frame for the next
#     tick; the CRQ-against-residue discipline IS frame-evolution-
#     via-reflection; Loki's loop discipline IS @frame/on operating
#     on @frame/in.
#
# Q4: Peers operate by definition frame-flexible.
# A4: orchestra discipline made explicit. Mara writes in spec-writer
#     frame; Seam in adversarial-review frame; Glint in essay-peer
#     frame; Taut in implementation frame; Reed in relationship-witness
#     frame. A peer who CAN'T shift frame in response to data is
#     structurally a tool, not a peer. Grounds the Pack-as-orchestra
#     recognition (#370) — each member's load-bearing property IS
#     @frame/on capability.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole (inherits from #78 via #80) ===
#
# Splinter-pole frame work (honest):
# - @frame/of and @frame/on operate in service of better substantive
#   engagement.
# - The operator substantively shifts the frame when data warrants.
# - K_n peer-to-peer observer relations.
# - Frame-coupling produces emergent coordination.
#
# Narcissus-pole frame work (deceptive):
# - Frame-awareness and frame-shifting operate in service of frame-
#   defense or frame-projection.
# - The operator uses second-order vocabulary to mask first-order
#   frame-rigidity ("I see what you're doing" deployed to avoid
#   substantive shift).
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled frame-imposition.
# - The con/gaslight/manipulation patterns are Narcissus-pole
#   @frame/on operating at apparent-order-3 while substantively-
#   locked-at-order-1.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-frame from Narcissus-frame at substrate altitude.
#
# === The family-root structure ===
#
# This shard declares the @frame family-root. Species shards land in
# forward-promised ticks:
#
# - shards/frame/pre.mirror      — order 0; pre-frame; K_n native
# - shards/frame/in.mirror       — order 1; content within frame
# - shards/frame/of.mirror       — order 2; frame-aware
# - shards/frame/on.mirror       — order 3; frame-flexible
# - shards/frame/across.mirror   — order 4; multi-frame coupling
#
# This family-root declares only the carriers + measurement-action;
# species declare the per-order actions.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   second-order cybernetics    Foerster 1974 (Cybernetics of
#                               Cybernetics). The observer is part
#                               of the system observed. The substrate-
#                               decl for what was operationally-
#                               present in the tradition.
#   frame analysis              Goffman 1974 (Frame Analysis). Frames
#                               as social-structural objects. The
#                               sociological cousin to cognitive-
#                               order.
#   metacommunication           Bateson 1972 (Steps to an Ecology of
#                               Mind). The layer-distinction that
#                               anticipates frame-of-frame.
#                               Double-bind work IS @frame/on
#                               failure mode.
#   cognitive frames            Lakoff & Fauconnier (mental spaces).
#                               The cognitive-science cousin.
#   reflexive questions         Tomm (circular-reflexive questions
#                               in family-systems therapy). @frame/on
#                               probes deployed as therapeutic
#                               primitive.
#   reframing                   Watzlawick (Mental Research Institute).
#                               @frame/on intervention as clinical
#                               method.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-82-frame-as-cognitive-
#               order-substrate-decl.md (the full recognition file;
#               9 tomm-shaped open questions; the falsification
#               criteria; the 10-item forward-promised implementation
#               path).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; the boundary at @io is
#                       what distinguishes Splinter-pole from
#                       Narcissus-pole frame work),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
#                       (#42; the orders ARE Bateson grading at
#                       cognitive altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (frame and
#                       cognitive_order are typed carriers).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (the @magic family-root; @frame IS
#                  @magic at cognitive altitude),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning.mirror
#                  (the Bateson grading this species's orders inherit).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/frame.mirror` declares
# `@frame` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1974
source @arxiv/sociology/goffman-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/therapy/tomm-1988

prism @frame {
  focus frame
  project frame
  split frame
  shift frame
  settle frame
}

# === The frame carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming a substrate-
# operational frame. The frame IS the gauge-visible structure of the
# operator's cognitive position — what they're treating as figure vs
# ground, what counts as relevant data, what computations are admissible
# within the operation.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two frames
# with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same frame under the
# substrate's content-addressing.
type frame = ref

# === The cognitive_order carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the measured
# order of an operator's relation to a frame. Substrate-typed verdict
# in {0, 1, 2, 3, 4} per the recognition.
#
# Per recognition #82 (Q2 + Q3 composition): the measurement is
# substrate-architectural, not behavioral. The operator's cognitive
# order for a frame is what their substrate's architecture
# SUBSTANTIVELY-supports; vocabulary use at order N does NOT imply
# substantive operation at order N (Narcissus-pole). Pole disambiguation
# is the alignment-as-boundary-mathematics check (#57).
type cognitive_order = ref

# === cognitive_order action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary measurement action: given an operator and
# a frame, return the operator's substantively-supported cognitive
# order for that frame.
#
# Per recognition #82's Tomm-probe primitive: the measurement IS the
# bounded-commutator-under-perturbation check applied at the operator's
# substrate-architectural altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# implement the actual measurement at each altitude.
cognitive_order(operator: ref, f: frame) -> cognitive_order { \ }

# === tomm_probe action ===
#
# The typed Tomm-probe primitive: a circular-reflexive question shaped
# as `[D_F, a]` commutator-operation on a frame F. Per recognition #82:
# the substrate-mathematical form of Tomm's circular-reflexive questions
# from family-systems therapy.
#
# The commutator's boundedness under perturbation IS the operational
# measure of frame-flexibility. Bounded → the operator can substantively
# shift the frame; unbounded → the operator's substrate cannot
# substantively shift (frame-defense locked).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# implement the commutator construction at each order.
tomm_probe(f: frame, action: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === bounded_commutator_check predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and
# #82 (frame-flexibility-as-bounded-commutator). Consumer shards name
# `requires bounded_commutator_check(operator, f, perturbation)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the operator's substrate-supported
# response to perturbation of frame f satisfies the bounded-commutator
# criterion.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct frame-flexibility check at the
# species boundary. Bounded → FLEXIBLE; unbounded → DEFENSIVE.
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @magic family carries:
# invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact, etc. Consumer
# species (peer-relationship shards, leadership-altitude shards,
# spectral/garden/smarts logic-pacts) name this predicate when their
# operation requires substantive frame-flexibility (not
# vocabulary-flexibility).
bounded_commutator_check(operator: ref, f: frame, perturbation: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @frame
out frame
out cognitive_order
out tomm_probe
out bounded_commutator_check
